# Each turn boxes the counter, one addition, and calls one stub with the map and the key in registers.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[wide]] = ZExt32(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[key]] = Add(b@[[wide]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int64 b@[[found]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[key]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# The answer comes back boxed. An integer and a double each take one test and one conversion; anything else is undefined, which travels as a marked NaN.
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isInteger]] = AboveEqual(b@[[found]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isInteger]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isMissing]] = GreaterEqual(b@{{*}}, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isMissing]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub and the poll of the loop are all that can leave the loop.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# CALLS: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS: isLoopPoll, ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
